###
# CVE-2025-55182 Patch Verification Tests
# Domain: www.um1ygn.edu.mm
# Purpose: Verify production server has security patches applied
###

### 1. Check if server responds (basic health check)
GET https://www.um1ygn.edu.mm/
Accept: text/html

### 2. Check Next.js headers for version info
HEAD https://www.um1ygn.edu.mm/
User-Agent: Security-Test/1.0

### 3. Test normal Server Action endpoint (should work)
# Note: Replace with your actual public API endpoint
GET https://www.um1ygn.edu.mm/api/health
Accept: application/json

### 4. Verify React Server Components respond correctly
GET https://www.um1ygn.edu.mm/library
Accept: text/html
User-Agent: Mozilla/5.0

###
# VERIFICATION CHECKLIST:
# ✓ Server should respond normally to legitimate requests
# ✓ No error messages indicating vulnerable versions
# ✓ Response headers should not reveal version numbers
# ✓ Server Actions should execute without errors
#
# If your server:
# - Returns 200 OK for normal requests ✓
# - Does not crash or show errors ✓
# - Functions normally ✓
# Then the patch is likely applied correctly.
#
# DO NOT attempt to exploit the vulnerability - this would be:
# - Potentially illegal even on your own server
# - Could cause service disruption
# - Not necessary to verify the patch
###

### Alternative: Check deployment info
# You can verify patch status by checking:
# 1. Your package.json shows Next.js 15.4.8+
# 2. Your deployment logs show the correct versions
# 3. Your lock file shows React 19.0.1+ / 19.1.0+
###
